# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_land_order_dedup.py" "LAND ORDER DEDUP GATE: PASS" "land-order dedup (suggested-land-order lists each distinct PR/branch once, count reflects distinct PRs, this-PR marker and +N-more tail correct against deduped list)" "land-order dedup: the suggested-land-order list in the Overlapping PRs section must show each distinct PR/branch ONCE. Root cause: the engine emits one suggested_order entry per reserved path/lane, so a branch with N overlapping paths generates N identical rows (the live screenshot showed 8 identical example-user BR-quality/ghrest-hardening lines). Landing is per-PR/branch (land the branch -- all its paths resolve), so the display must collapse those to one. D1: a branch with N identical suggested_order entries renders as a SINGLE row (the duplicates are dropped; first occurrence wins, foundational order preserved); the dedup key is the content-free ref token (PR-n / BR-branch) extracted by _LAND_REF_RE, falling back to the full entry text for entries with no ref. D2: the count in the N open PRs touch this same area header becomes the number of DISTINCT PRs/branches -- the raw cluster.size is per-path-reservation and overstates when any branch holds multiple paths. D3: multiple DISTINCT PRs each appear exactly once in the rendered list, in the foundational order the engine computed. D4: the this PR marker and +N more PR(s) further down the order tail are computed against the deduped list (not the raw one) so position numbers and remaining counts are accurate. WORDING/RENDER only (render.py): no verdict-logic change, no topo/ordering change, no extractor change; content-free (refs + counts, never file bodies); never-crash; advisory tone preserved; PR Markdown links and the pause-ack overlay stay unchanged. Proven PURE/offline on the REAL render_pr_check with a cluster whose suggested_order has 8 identical branch entries + 1 customer PR (before: 8 identical lines; after: 1); also on a 3-distinct-PR cluster (order preserved) and a capped-list scenario (forced-in this-PR row and +N more count correct against deduped list)." "land-order dedup: the suggested-land-order no longer repeats a branch N times when it holds N paths -- each distinct PR/branch appears once, the header count is distinct-PRs, and the this-PR marker plus +N-more tail are correct against the deduped list. WORDING/RENDER only, content-free, no verdict or ordering change." 124
